{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790327699,"nonce":"Hd4roI9ilvjosxeBTg1oeW/tOVc=","title":"Frontend workarounds for control flow in block values can go","message":"With 1556c83 and 19c227b fixed, a TypedExpression::Block used as a value lowers `if`, loops, `break` and `continue` the way a function body does, including a `break`/`continue` that leaves a loop around the block. The frontends route around the old defects in these places, which were left alone in the fix:\n\n- Python `Lowerer::conditional_value` (crates/zyntax_python/src/lower.rs): a ternary or `and`/`or` whose branch has statements is lowered as an `if` statement assigning a temp, hoisted to the enclosing statement (b8d66e6, 5b4a0c1).\n- Python comprehension rewrites around `flag and len([x for x in xs])` / `flag and list(x for x in xs)` (19c227b's reproducers, b8d66e6).\n- Python checked tuple unbox without guards picks by an if expression instead of an if statement in a block value (0f0e5585, 382b32e).\n- Lua debug `after_call` (crates/zyntax_lua/src/lower.rs): the read-back of locals a callee set is straight-line `zl_dbg_pick` calls rather than `if (set \u0026 1) != 0 { a = list[0] }`, because the call may sit in an expression.\n\nEach can return to the direct shape once measured: the direct shape may be cheaper (no hoisted temp, no pick call per local) or may not; decide per site with the A/B.","files":null}]}